From 3a1d75f3494a0233aad52302d43ba2c277c13550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] execution observations: date a remote running card
 by its executor's heartbeat events

Under links_reader=replica (every host), a card on another gateway came from the Board
replica with no run identity, so every remote card projected unknown /
missing_qualified_identity in /api/session-kanban-tasks, the sidebar counts and
session-idle-check (Mac readback t_01a1cfc6ea23e588 on hub card t_01a1c7a649c59bec).

The replica already carries source-owned liveness: the executor writes heartbeat
(and claimed/spawned) task events with its own created_at and a portable uid, and
they sync everywhere. For a running replica card whose current run is running and
unended, the newest such event of THAT run dates a v1 card observation:
identity gateway/profile/board/work_id + run_id = the run's portable uid,
observed_at = event created_at, valid_until +180 s, revision event:<uid>.

- Never the pull clock: a fresh pull of an old heartbeat expires on time alone.
- Old-run, ended/released runs, parked cards, future clocks and a profile the
  origin ledger does not name (the 'default' label) stay explicit unknown.
- Stale replica: unknown/source_unavailable with last_known_state running.
- The counts (sidebar) evidence sink gets the same raw record as session_tasks.
- Two correlated subqueries evaluated only for running rows (task_runs PK,
  task_events(run_id,id) index): ~20 ms for 92 real links, unchanged from base.

Parked replica cards keep their explicit unknown: the replica has no executor
clock for them.
